### Sistema de Gestão de Tarefas - Azure Functions .NET 8
### Base URL para desenvolvimento local
@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071/api

### Variáveis globais - Atualize conforme necessário
@taskId = 
@taskId2 = 
@taskId3 = 

###############################################################################
### HEALTH CHECKS - Sempre teste primeiro
###############################################################################

### 1. Health Check básico
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Health Check detalhado (com estatísticas)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/detailed
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
### CRUD DE TAREFAS - Operações Básicas
###############################################################################

### 3. Listar todas as tarefas (deve estar vazio inicialmente)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Criar primeira tarefa - Completa
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Implementar autenticação JWT",
  "description": "Desenvolver sistema de autenticação usando JWT para APIs",
  "assignedTo": "developer@empresa.com",
  "tags": ["segurança", "jwt", "alta-prioridade"]
}

### Copie o ID retornado e cole na variável @taskId acima

###

### 5. Criar segunda tarefa - Simples
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Revisar documentação da API",
  "description": "Atualizar documentação com novos endpoints"
}

### Copie o ID retornado e cole na variável @taskId2 acima

###

### 6. Criar terceira tarefa - Para testes de workflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Configurar pipeline CI/CD",
  "description": "Implementar deploy automático com GitHub Actions",
  "assignedTo": "devops@empresa.com",
  "tags": ["devops", "cicd", "automação"]
}

### Copie o ID retornado e cole na variável @taskId3 acima

###

### 7. Obter tarefa por ID específico
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Listar todas as tarefas (agora deve ter 3 tarefas)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
### ATUALIZAÇÕES DE TAREFAS
###############################################################################

### 9. Atualizar apenas o status para InProgress
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "InProgress"
}

###

### 10. Atualizar múltiplos campos
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Revisar e atualizar documentação da API",
  "description": "Atualizar documentação com novos endpoints e exemplos de uso",
  "status": "InProgress",
  "assignedTo": "tech-writer@empresa.com",
  "tags": ["documentação", "api", "exemplos"]
}

###

### 11. Marcar tarefa como concluída
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId3}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Completed"
}

###

### 12. Verificar se a data de conclusão foi definida
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId3}}
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
### FILTROS POR STATUS - Teste todos os status possíveis
###############################################################################

### 13. Buscar tarefas pendentes
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/status/Pending
Accept: application/json

###

### 14. Buscar tarefas em progresso
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/status/InProgress
Accept: application/json

###

### 15. Buscar tarefas concluídas
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/status/Completed
Accept: application/json

###

### 16. Buscar tarefas canceladas (deve estar vazio)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/status/Cancelled
Accept: application/json

###

### 17. Cancelar uma tarefa para testar filtro
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Cancelled"
}

###

### 18. Buscar tarefas canceladas novamente
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/status/Cancelled
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
### TESTES DE VALIDAÇÃO - Casos que devem falhar
###############################################################################

### 19. Teste - Criar tarefa sem título (deve falhar)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Tarefa sem título para testar validação"
}

###

### 20. Teste - Criar tarefa com título muito longo (deve falhar)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.",
  "description": "Teste de validação de título longo"
}

###

